+- `provenanceAt(area, x, y)` → a copy of the burning cell's provenance or `null`. `fire(fireId)` / `fires()` → the fire summaries kept in `state.fire.fires`: `{ fireId, startedAt, startedOn, sourceType, sourceObjectId, sourceCell, firstFuelIgnited, cause, area, cells (ever lit), burning (now), out (beat the last cell went out, else null), casualties: [{ unitId, name, beat, cell, spreadSteps }] }`; the newest 64 finished fires are kept, burning ones always. `describeProvenance(prov)` → "Burned to death by fire fire-3 originating from open_fire (campfire) at (20, 20, 0) via 2 spread steps". `burningCells()` entries carry `fireId`.
+- **Casualties.** A unit that dies in a burning cell gets `data.fireProvenance` (a copy) and `data.deathCause = "fire"`, is appended to the fire's `casualties`, and is handed to `UF.DeathForensics.recordDeath(unit, "fire")` before `UF.Combat.onUnitDeath` (whose own recordDeath call is the second one and does nothing). `DEUS_DeathForensics` puts the provenance on the record (`record.fireProvenance`, `record.fireDeathText`, the ring-buffer event `burned to death`) and prints it with the `[DEATH FORENSICS]` line.
